# Identify, research, fix assumptions

This is a Cursor **project rule** (`alwaysApply: true`), not a skill. It is injected when this file is on the checkout. Applies to **every code change** (implement, fix, refactor, Launch Control, tests). Skip only when the user asked a question and you make **no edits**.

## Identify

Before/while editing, list the assumptions the change relies on. Silent guesses are not allowed. Typical in this repo: OS, paths, SDK, process model, UI binding, “this file/folder always exists”, MLC layout, in-memory-only, Windows-only, test host.

## Research

Verify each against repo code, README, tests, and nearby docs. Grep/read; do not invent. If you cannot verify, say so and pick the safer encoding. Launch Control changes must also match the Master Launch Control contract (scan `*LaunchControl*.cmd`, Generic sidecar, no `start ""`, `LaunchControl.Standard` discovery). A README or comment that disagrees with the code is a false assumption.

## Fix

Do not ship a known-false or unverified assumption. Encode reality: validation, fallback, correct path/API, or a test that locks the contract. Comments-only is not a fix.

After the change, re-scan for assumptions you just introduced and fix those too.

Do not dump a long assumptions essay in the PR unless something surprising was found. The work product is corrected code + tests.
